Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
; VibeForge Systems - Windows Environment Bundle
; explorerpatcher.reg - ExplorerPatcher (EP) profile
;
; EP stores all of its settings under HKCU\Software\ExplorerPatcher. These
; values restore a Windows 10-style shell on Windows 11. Every value is
; documented and reversible.
;
; TO REVERT: delete the HKCU\Software\ExplorerPatcher key (or open EP's
; "Properties" UI and choose "Restore default settings"), then restart Explorer.
;
; NOTE: EP exposes far more options through its settings UI. This file pins
; only the load-bearing choices so a fresh workstation lands deterministically.
; ============================================================================

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\ExplorerPatcher]
; Use the Windows 10 taskbar instead of the Windows 11 one (1 = Win10 taskbar).
"OldTaskbar"=dword:00000001
; Combine taskbar buttons / always show labels off -> classic grouping (0 = always combine).
"TaskbarGlomLevel"=dword:00000000
; Mitigations that keep the classic taskbar stable after Windows updates.
"ClassicThemeMitigations"=dword:00000001
; Show the classic (Windows 10) Start menu shell, deferring the menu itself to Open-Shell.
"Start_ShowClassicMode"=dword:00000001
; Disable the Windows 11 immersive context menu in the taskbar/Start surfaces.
"ImmersiveContextMenu"=dword:00000000
; Restore the Windows 10 Alt+Tab window switcher.
"AltTabWindows"=dword:00000000
; Use the classic battery / network / volume flyouts.
"OldNetworkFlyout"=dword:00000001
"OldSoundFlyout"=dword:00000001
